@startuml state-slides-modes
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because a PDF view's slide-deck modes are a small state machine whose states are held in
'' different places and whose transitions have different initiators — and both are meant to be read off the
'' colours. A PlantUML state diagram gives composite states, choice pseudo-states, per-state fills and
'' per-transition arrow colours from the shared palette, and it renders byte-reproducibly; Mermaid's does not.
'' Fills: teal = held by the PDF engine (renderer.pdf: its :layout and the slide it shows); blue-violet = an app-db
'' key ([:ui :presentation], [:ui :slides :digits|:blank|:overview?]). Arrows: magenta = a key only; blue = a
'' command reachable from keys, menus, the toolbar, the slide bar, the context menu or the palette (a re-frame
'' event); slate = the window (main's vv:fullscreen-changed); teal = the view itself (mount, unmount, and the layout a
'' show returns to, deck/effective-layout).
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title A PDF view's modes (ADR-0045, ADR-0048): the Document layout, the Slides layout, and Presenting

hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor RENDERER_TINT
}

state "a PDF view is mounted (vinary.ui.views/pdf-view → renderer.pdf controller)" as View RENDERER_FILL {

  state "Document layout\ncontinuous pages · zoom and Fit apply" as Document RENDERER_TINT

  state "Slides layout, in a tab\none slide per screen · 16 px margin" as Slides RENDERER_TINT {
    state "Showing slide p" as SShow RENDERER_TINT
    state "Typing a slide number\n[:ui :slides :digits]" as SDigits APPDB_TINT
    state "Overview grid open\n[:ui :slides :overview?]" as SOver APPDB_TINT
    [*] --> SShow
    SShow -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> SDigits : 0–9
    SDigits -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> SShow : Enter · Escape ·\n2.5 s idle · a slide step
    SShow -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> SOver : Tab · o · Slide Overview ·\nthe slide bar's grid button
    SOver -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> SShow : Escape · Tab · o ·\nopen a tile (a jump)
  }

  state "Presenting — a slide show\n[:ui :presentation] · .vv-root.vv-presenting only when chromeless:\nnot in a linked show's presenter window, which keeps its chrome" as Present APPDB_FILL {
    state "Showing slide p\nno margin · a click advances ·\nchromeless: chrome hidden, idle pointer hides" as PShow RENDERER_TINT
    state "Blanked black or white\n[:ui :slides :blank]" as PBlank APPDB_TINT
    state "Typing a slide number\n[:ui :slides :digits]" as PDigits APPDB_TINT
    state "Overview grid open\n[:ui :slides :overview?]" as POver APPDB_TINT
    [*] --> PShow : :from — the first slide,\nthe current one, or a page
    PShow -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> PBlank : b · . (black)\nw · , (white)
    PBlank -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> PShow : the same key · a slide step\n(it only unblanks) · click · Escape
    PShow -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> PDigits : 0–9
    PDigits -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> PShow : Enter · Escape ·\n2.5 s idle · a slide step
    PShow -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> POver : Tab · o · palette
    POver -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> PShow : Escape · Tab · o ·\nopen a tile (a jump)
  }

  state mountChoice <<choice>>
  state stopChoice <<choice>>

  [*] -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> mountChoice : mount\n(deck/effective-layout)
  mountChoice -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> Slides : a detected deck and\n:slides-open-as :slides,\nor this view's choice :slides
  mountChoice -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> Document : otherwise

  Document -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> Slides : View as Slide Show (l) ·\ntoolbar · context menu
  Slides -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> Document : View as Document (m) ·\ntoolbar · context menu
  Document -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> Present : F5 · Shift+F5 ·\nStart Slide Show ·\nStart From This Slide
  Slides -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> Present : F5 · Shift+F5 ·\nPresent (slide bar)

  PShow -[KEYMAP_BORDER]-> stopChoice : Escape — the last step
  Present -[REFRAME_BORDER]-> stopChoice : End Slide Show (also the View menu) ·\nfocusing the address bar or sidebar\n(a chromeless window only)
  Present -[MAIN_BORDER,dashed]-> stopChoice : a chromeless window left the\nfullscreen the show asked for
  stopChoice -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> Slides : a deck, or this view's\nchoice is :slides
  stopChoice -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> Document : otherwise
}

View -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> [*] : unmount — a tab switch, navigation, Reflow\n(:slides/unmounted also ends a show — but a linked\nshow's presenter, its show tab still open, goes AWAY:\nthe show runs on in the audience window, ADR-0048 §8.10)

note left of View #FFF6D6
  **Escape unwinds one step at a time**
  (vinary.input.events/escape-fx), after the
  palette and the find bar:
  overview → typed number → blanking → the show.
  The show ends only in its own view; in a window
  that keeps its chrome, an Escape from a text
  field or a bar leaves the show's steps alone.
  Ending a show leaves only a fullscreen
  main entered (vinary.main.fullscreen/decide).
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Fill: where the state is held · Arrow: what triggers it |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| fill: the PDF engine (renderer.pdf :layout, the slide shown) · arrow: the view itself — mount, unmount, the layout a show returns to |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| fill: an app-db key ([:ui :presentation], [:ui :slides …]) |
  |<#BC6EC5>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| arrow: a key only (the :slides keymap layer, Escape) |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| arrow: a command — keys, menus, toolbar, slide bar, context menu or palette |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| arrow (dashed): the window — main reports vv:fullscreen-changed |
endlegend
@enduml
